# Cloudflare Pages — Custom HTTP headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# (Netlify also supports this file format, so it works on both platforms.)
#
# ── THE CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY IS ENFORCED NOW ─────────────────────────────
#
# It used to be four directives — frame-ancestors, object-src, base-uri,
# upgrade-insecure-requests — with the long, carefully built policy sitting on
# the Report-Only header where it constrained nothing. So nothing stopped a
# script injected into checkout.html from reading the page around the card
# frame and posting it somewhere else. That is the specific control a PCI
# SAQ-A-EP questionnaire asks about, and the answer was "we are thinking about
# it".
#
# WHAT HAD TO BE FIXED BEFORE IT COULD BE TURNED ON. The report-only policy was
# not correct — it had never been enforced, so nothing had ever caught its
# gaps. Three script hosts the site genuinely uses were missing from it, found
# by walking every browser-side file for both static <script src> and
# dynamically assigned .src (the second is where the third-party SDKs live, and
# a scan that only reads HTML misses all of them):
#
#     www.paypal.com      paypal-button.js — the PayPal SDK.  Promoting the
#                         policy as written would have broken PayPal checkout.
#     cdn.jsdelivr.net    admin-finance.js (Chart.js), builder.html (QRious)
#     unpkg.com           analytics.html (React UMD builds)
#
# tests/csp-is-enforced-and-complete.test.js now walks the same files on every
# run, so the next SDK somebody adds fails in CI rather than on checkout.
#
# WHAT IS STILL LOOSE, DELIBERATELY. script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' and
# 'unsafe-eval'. Every page in this repository has inline handlers and inline
# pre-paint blocks, so removing it is a real piece of work — hashes or a nonce
# on every one of them — and shipping that in the same change as the promotion
# would mean a broken storefront and no way to tell which half did it.
#
# So the enforced policy stops a script being LOADED from a host nobody
# allowlisted, which is how skimmers actually arrive, and does not yet stop one
# being injected inline. That is a real improvement and a partial one, and it
# is written down rather than implied.
#
# WHERE THE REPORT-ONLY HEADER POINTS NOW. At the next step, not at the one
# just taken: it is the same policy WITHOUT 'unsafe-inline' and 'unsafe-eval'.
# /api/csp-report therefore collects exactly the list of inline blocks that
# have to be given a hash before that can be enforced too. A report-only copy
# of a policy already enforced would collect nothing and teach nothing.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: payment=(*)
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://js.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com https://www.paypal.com https://*.paypal.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://connect.facebook.net https://*.posthog.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://www.clarity.ms https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://client.crisp.chat https://embed.tawk.to https://s.pinimg.com https://analytics.tiktok.com https://plausible.io https://widget.trustpilot.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://api.stripe.com https://*.paypal.com https://*.posthog.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://*.facebook.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.github.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.clarity.ms https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://client.crisp.chat wss://client.relay.crisp.chat https://*.tawk.to wss://*.tawk.to https://ct.pinterest.com https://analytics.tiktok.com https://plausible.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.google.com https://www.googleadservices.com; media-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co blob: data: https://*.r2.dev; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://client.crisp.chat https://embed.tawk.to; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com https://client.crisp.chat; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: https://*.r2.dev; frame-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com https://www.paypal.com https://*.paypal.com https://*.facebook.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://td.doubleclick.net https://widget.trustpilot.com https://*.tawk.to https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.tiktok.com https://www.instagram.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self' https://*.paypal.com https://*.stripe.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests; report-uri /api/csp-report
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com https://www.paypal.com https://*.paypal.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://connect.facebook.net https://*.posthog.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://www.clarity.ms https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://client.crisp.chat https://embed.tawk.to https://s.pinimg.com https://analytics.tiktok.com https://plausible.io https://widget.trustpilot.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://api.stripe.com https://*.paypal.com https://*.posthog.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://*.facebook.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.github.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.clarity.ms https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://client.crisp.chat wss://client.relay.crisp.chat https://*.tawk.to wss://*.tawk.to https://ct.pinterest.com https://analytics.tiktok.com https://plausible.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.google.com https://www.googleadservices.com; media-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co blob: data: https://*.r2.dev; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://client.crisp.chat https://embed.tawk.to; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com https://client.crisp.chat; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: https://*.r2.dev; frame-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com https://*.stripe.com https://www.paypal.com https://*.paypal.com https://*.facebook.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://td.doubleclick.net https://widget.trustpilot.com https://*.tawk.to https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.tiktok.com https://www.instagram.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self' https://*.paypal.com https://*.stripe.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; report-uri /api/csp-report
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Allow analytics.html to be embedded as an iframe within the same site (admin dashboard)
# Both rules needed — CF Pages serves analytics.html at /analytics (pretty URL) too
/analytics
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/analytics.html
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Allow sizeguide to be embedded as an iframe in the product page size modal
# CF Pages serves sizeguide.html at /sizeguide (pretty URL) — both rules needed
/sizeguide
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/sizeguide.html
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

# Build id for the client auto-reload — must never be cached so an open tab can
# detect a new deploy (version-check in header-scroll.js).
/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Fonts are versioned + never change under a URL → cache hard like js/css.
/*.ttf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.otf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Vector/icon assets — small, effectively static; a month's cache, revalidate after.
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Raster images + video — a month's cache. NOT immutable on purpose: image URLs are
# hand-versioned (?v=N), not auto-hashed like js/css, so a revalidate-after-a-month
# window means a swapped image can never be stuck stale indefinitely.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.avif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.gif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.webm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.mov
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Apple Pay domain verification file (required by Stripe / Apple Pay)
/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Cache-Control: no-cache
